@startuml
!include ../../../../../../plantuml/sodexo-theme.puml

title Amend or cancel a reservation — Submit the authorised change
header Sat, 25 Jul 2026 · End-to-end discovery sequence
footer (c) Developed by <b>Mohit Kanwar</b>

hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 90

actor "Booking Operator" as Actor
participant "Booking Operations Workspace" as Surface
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Accommodation Experience API" as Edge
participant "Booking.com Integration Service" as Service1
database "Service-owned data" as Data
queue "Kafka event platform" as Events
participant "Booking.com Demand API" as BookingCom #FBDADD


group 1. Submit an authorised accommodation modification.
  Actor -> Surface: Submit an authorised accommodation modification
  Surface -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/bookings/{bookingId}/modifications
  Gateway -> Edge: JWT, tenant scope, correlation ID
  Edge -> Service1: Submit an authorised accommodation modification.
  alt authorised and valid
  Service1 -> Service1: Validate transition and persist
  Service1 -> BookingCom: POST /3.2/orders/modify
  BookingCom --> Service1: Supplier response + request_id
  Service1 -> Events: Publish committed domain event
  Service1 --> Edge: Accepted state and next actions
  Edge --> Surface: Response envelope
  Surface --> Actor: Updated journey state
else validation, state, or dependency failure
  Service1 --> Edge: Problem details + retryability
  Edge --> Surface: Safe error and next action
  Surface --> Actor: Correct, retry later, or escalate
end
end

group 2. Submit an authorised cancellation with fee acknowledgement.
  Actor -> Surface: Submit an authorised cancellation with fee acknowledgement
  Surface -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/bookings/{bookingId}/cancellations
  Gateway -> Edge: JWT, tenant scope, correlation ID
  Edge -> Service1: Submit an authorised cancellation with fee acknowledgement.
  alt authorised and valid
  Service1 -> Service1: Validate transition and persist
  Service1 -> BookingCom: POST /3.2/orders/cancel
  BookingCom --> Service1: Supplier response + request_id
  Service1 -> Events: Publish committed domain event
  Service1 --> Edge: Accepted state and next actions
  Edge --> Surface: Response envelope
  Surface --> Actor: Updated journey state
else validation, state, or dependency failure
  Service1 --> Edge: Problem details + retryability
  Edge --> Surface: Safe error and next action
  Surface --> Actor: Correct, retry later, or escalate
end
end

@enduml
